                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Talismania Game Review\r\n(Disclaimer - This is just my opinion and may be unpopular or disliked.)\r\n\r\n(Positive)\r\n1. It is a rather short game consisting of only 8 levels in total.\r\n2. It teaches some Greek mythology when playing the mini-games between levels.\r\n3. It is on the one hand really relaxing to play and certain visuals and sounds add to this, but can become frustrating if your end goal is a \"perfect\" run.\r\n4. It is not hard to understand or learn to play.\r\n5. If you like Tile-Matchhing games this is a really good one.\r\n6. The art style is very cute.\r\n\r\n(Negative)\r\n1. If you do a \"pefect\" run you will notice the game getting progressively harder as you get closer to the end, which can be frustrating as it no longer has a relaxing-casual feel all the time.\r\n2. I wish there were more levels as it really was nice.\r\n3. If you you don't like Tile-Matching games this won't be for you.",
